Extra Features
None, the program implements only required functionality.

Known Bugs
No known bugs.

Lessons Learned
This assignment helped us understand how the choice of disk scheduling algorithm affects how far the disk arm has to move. Writing FCFS first gave us a baseline, and it was clear right away that it moves the arm much more than the others because it never reorders the requests. SSF was straightforward but we could see how it can jump back and forth as long as the next request is close. The elevator took the most thought because we had to handle reversing direction once there were no more requests ahead and make sure the arm stopped at the last request instead of running to the end of the disk. Testing against the example from the textbook gave us confidence that our totals were being calculated correctly. We also learned to seed rand() only once so the sequence is not the same every time the program starts.
